WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.595
Inside histogram, partial holds four counters shared by one four-thread block.

00:00:05.595 --> 00:00:10.225
Each thread clears one counter; a barrier precedes atomic updates.

00:00:10.225 --> 00:00:18.660
A second barrier completes those updates before nonzero partials are added to the global counts. main initialises global counts to zero.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.105
Initialise counters.

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:24.205
Clear shared and global counts.

00:00:24.205 --> 00:00:25.910
Count atomically.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:28.980
Several threads may target the same category.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.365
Merge partials.

00:00:30.365 --> 00:00:33.035
Add completed per-block counts globally.

00:00:34.535 --> 00:00:40.505
Per-block shared counters combine local contributions before a merge to device-memory counters.

00:00:40.505 --> 00:00:47.610
An atomic update protects one supported update; it does not replace the block barriers around initialisation and merging.
